Quick operational examples & tuning guidance (summary)
    • If DE5 controller overshoots currents frequently: reduce k_t_base or increase I_sat (if you know the real magnetic knee is higher).
    • If currents often exceed I_cont, use a scheduling policy: allow peak_mode only for brief durations (few seconds) then force cool-down.
    • Use graphite_spreader thermal_resistance ~ 5e-4 K/W in your approximation to see realistic thermal margins (we used values like 0.0005 K/W in the earlier analysis).
    • For ribbon wire: reduce R_winding by estimated factor (higher fill factor) — implement as variable conductor_resistivity_factor in eval_motor_proxy.